        "estimatedTime": "10s",
        "config": {
          "prompt": "Theme: Animal Saving Story\nDuration: 30 seconds\nScenes: 3 scenes × 10 seconds\nStyle: Cinematic, emotional, realistic, short-film\n\n🎞️ SCENE 1 (0–10 seconds) — Danger Introduced\n\nShow a tense situation where a helpless life is stuck (randomly choose each time):\n\na child trapped near water\n\nan elderly person collapsed on a road\n\na baby animal caught in debris\n\nVisuals:\n\nRealistic environment (street, village, forest, flood area)\n\nWorried expressions, slow dramatic camera movement\n\nSound of danger (rain, traffic, rushing water)\n\nMood: Fear, urgency, silence broken by tension\n\n🎞️ SCENE 2 (10–20 seconds) — The Rescue\n\nA dog notices the danger and takes action.\nShow the dog:\n\nrunning fast\n\nbarking for help OR\n\npulling, pushing, blocking danger, or guiding humans\n\nVisuals:\n\nSlow-motion shots\n\nClose-up of the dog’s determined eyes\n\nFast cuts showing effort, struggle, and bravery\n\nMood: Courage, hope, rising emotional music\n\n🎞️ SCENE 3 (20–30 seconds) — Life Saved\n\nThe stuck life is successfully saved.\nHumans arrive or the danger passes.\n\nVisuals:\n\nThe rescued life breathing safely\n\nPeople emotional, grateful\n\nThe dog calm, standing silently or walking away\n\nEnding Shot:\nText on screen:\n\n“Sometimes heroes walk on four legs.”\n\nMood: Relief, warmth, emotional closure",
          "systemPrompt": "Ultra-realistic visuals\n\nNatural lighting\n\nEmotional cinematic background score\n\nNo narration (story told visually)\n\nHigh emotional impact suitable for YouTube Shorts",
          "temperature": 0.7,
          "concatPrompts": false
        },
